  <body>
    <front><contents /></front>
    <chapter>
      <heading>
        Software documentation for the TTIONameTokenizerV2
        class
      </heading>
      <class name="TTIONameTokenizerV2" super="NSObject">
        <declared>TTIONameTokenizerV2.h</declared>
        <desc>
          <em>Description forthcoming.</em>
        </desc>
        <method type="NSString*" factory="yes">
          <sel>backendName</sel>
          <desc>
            Backend identifier string describing the active
            implementation. @return `@"native"` when
            `libttio_rans` is linked; reserved for
            future fallback identifiers.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSArray&lt;NSString*&gt;*" factory="yes">
          <sel>decodeData:</sel>
          <arg type="NSData*">blob</arg>
          <sel>error:</sel>
          <arg type="NSError**">error</arg>
          <desc>
            Decode a NAME_TOKENIZED v2 <var>blob</var> back into
            its read-name list. Inverse of `+encodeNames:`.
            Verifies the v2 magic and version before decoding;
            bad framing populates `*error`. @param <var>blob</var>
            Encoded codec-15 channel bytes. @param
            <var>error</var> Out-error on bad magic, unknown
            version, or decode failure. @return Read names in
            record order, or `nil` with `*error` set.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="NSData*" factory="yes">
          <sel>encodeNames:</sel>
          <arg type="NSArray&lt;NSString*&gt;*">names</arg>
          <desc>
            Encode an ordered list of ASCII read
            <var>names</var> to a NAME_TOKENIZED v2 blob.
            Column-aware tokeniser: splits each name on
            `:` / `_` / `.` / `#`, then rANS-encodes the per-column
            streams. Empty input yields an empty blob. @param
            <var>names</var> Read <var>names</var> in record
            order. ASCII only. @return Encoded blob bytes ready
            to be stored as the codec-15 channel.
          </desc>
        </method>
        <method type="BOOL" factory="yes">
          <sel>nativeAvailable</sel>
          <desc>
            Whether the native `libttio_rans` name-tokenizer v2
            entries are usable. Returns <code>YES</code> iff
            `libttio_rans` is linked and the
            `ttio_name_tok_v2_encode` /
            `_decode` symbols are reachable. @return
            <code>YES</code> if the native codec is available,
            <code>NO</code> otherwise.
          </desc>
        </method>
      </class>
    </chapter>
